course: dictionary
lesson: 13792
title: Always the same
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Invariable means never changing. It is always the same. Look at the word inside it: in- means not, and variable means able to change. So invariable means not able to change.
explain: «Dad's invariable breakfast is toast with honey.» Every morning it is the same breakfast. He never changes it. The word tells you he always has it.
explain: In grammar, some nouns are invariable. «One sheep» and «two sheep» look exactly the same. The word does not change its form for many. Deer and fish work the same way.
explain: Invariably is the adverb. «He invariably arrives early» means he always arrives early. Use the clues in the sentence to check: if the meaning is always, you have it right.
fact: Invariable means never changing, always the same.
fact: In- means not, and variable means able to change, so invariable means not able to change.
fact: «Sheep», «deer» and «fish» are invariable nouns: the plural has the same form as the singular.
fact: «Invariably» means always, as in «She invariably wears her red coat».
fact: In maths, an invariant is a value that stays the same when other things change. This is a rare, special use of the word.
exercise: «Mum's invariable breakfast is toast with honey.» What does invariable mean here? | *Always the same | Sometimes changing | Very big | Burnt
exercise: Why is «sheep» called an invariable noun? | It always changes its spelling | It is a farm animal | *It has the same form for one and for many | It is a very long word
exercise: «He invariably arrives early.» What does invariably mean? | *Always | Never | Quickly | Sometimes
test: «The school rule is invariable: coats go on the hooks.» What does invariable tell you? | The rule is only for Mondays | *The rule never changes | The rule is a question | The rule is new
test: Which of these is an invariable noun? | *sheep | cat | dogs | houses
exam: Which word is the opposite of invariable? | Always | *Variable | Constant | Same
